! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Bisbas et al. (2015) sec 5.4 H II region + PDR, at the ownership
! configuration D-190 is DOCUMENTED as having been run with, with the D-118
! availFrac stand-down REVERTED and nothing else changed (D-191 asks for
! exactly this build).
!
! D-196. The D-190/D-193/D-195 runs were made against an input file that
! was never committed - no fixture under benchmarks/pdr/ sets a single
! ownership keyword, so `hiipdr` runs on the compiled defaults, which are
! NOT what D-191 describes ("every fixture here sets that keyword to 1").
! This fixture reconstructs the documented configuration so D-191's open
! question can be asked of a state that is in the repository.
!
! It is a RECONSTRUCTION, not a recovery: pdrIonFromMocassin is the only
! ownership keyword D-191 names, so it is the only one set here. If other
! switches were also set in that lost input, this will differ from D-190
! and the difference is itself worth knowing.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
TStellar 40000.
contShape blackbody
LPhot 4.26e13
symmetricXYZ
Hdensity 100.
nebComposition "input/abunV1.in"
TeStart 8000.
maxIterateMC 22 90.
nPhotons 6000000
nx 31
ny 31
nz 31
nbins 600
nuMax 15.
nuMin 1.001e-5
Rin 30.e17
Rout 6.0e19
edges 6.0e19 6.0e19 6.0e19
convLimit 0.10
dustFile 'input/dust_species.dat' 'input/dust_sizes.dat'
MdMg constant 0.011295
pdr 1
pdrDataDir "/home/hmonteiro/software/mocassin_HM_2026_3DPDR/dataPDR"
pdrNetwork "reduced"
pdrZeta 5.0e-17
pdrCoolants 4 "12co.dat" "12c+.dat" "12c.dat" "16o.dat"
pdrStartIter 4
! MOCASSIN's ionization ratio is imposed on the network before and after
! each solve (D-162). This also disables the pdrOwnIon gate, whose test is
! `pdrOwnIon /= 0 .and. pdrIonFromMocassin == 0` (D-169), so ionBalance
! writes H/He/C/O/Mg in PDR cells again - which is the configuration in
! which the availFrac question below has any effect at all.
pdrIonFromMocassin 1
! D-118's stand-down, left AS IT IS AT D-190. The paired run flips this to
! 0 and changes nothing else.
ionChemRates 0
